 "note": [
  "Scripture is the Indian Revised Version (IRV, irvhin), the Hindi Bible the corpus quotes; Take Root was egress-blocked, so the whole IRV was parsed from the ebible mirror (bibles/hin_irv/usx, 31,104 verses) and pasted verbatim, with its baked-in cross-reference parentheticals dropped.",
  "A row is `mined` only when an exact byte substring of at least 45 characters of the IRV verse (or the whole verse, if shorter) stands in the Hindi chapter that quotes it. Verses deliberately departed from are `self_rendered` regardless: where Taylor's commentary depends on his RV reading (Song 2:6 present tense, 6:12 'chariots of my willing people', 7:9, 8:2 'that Thou mightest instruct me', 8:5-6 citron tree and seal on the arm, 1:5 split into a dialogue, 2:3 citron), where the IRV's feminine speaker becomes the Bridegroom's 'I adjure you' (2:7, 3:5, 8:4), where Proverbs 1 is voiced as the Lord rather than Wisdom (1:23, 1:26), and 2 Corinthians 3:18, which Taylor glosses inline.",
  "Citations follow the corrected English: Section II's exhortation is Psalm 45:10-11 (the English read 'Ps. xiv'; fixed in BODY_CORRECTIONS in the same PR, with the es/pt/sw/fr/am editions)."
 ],
